                <li><b>Comfort: </b>Spacious seating, Wi-Fi, power outlets, café car (Amtrak), quiet cars available</li>
                <li><b>Flexibility:</b> Direct city-center to city-center service with departures nearly every hour</li>
                <li><b>Pros:</b> Fastest overall travel time, no traffic stress, arrives directly downtown, scenic views of the corridor.</li>
                <li><b>Cons:</b> Amtrak can be pricey last-minute; MARC has limited weekend service; parking at Penn Station can be expensive</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Bus </h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Duration:</b> ~1 hour to 1.5 hours, depending on traffic</li>
                <li><b>Comfort:</b> Standard coach seating, basic Wi-Fi on some carriers (Greyhound, Megabus, FlixBus)</li>
                <li><b>Flexibility:</b> Multiple operators with various pickup points throughout both cities</li>
                <li><b>Pros: </b>Often cheaper than Amtrak; frequent schedules; multiple departure points</li>
                <li><b>Cons: </b>Subject to highway traffic (especially I-95); less comfortable than trains; limited space for luggage; not always city-center to city-center</li>
            </ul>
